{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/967098-5-things-for-a-mage-to-encounter","id":967098,"title":"[5 Things] for a Mage to encounter.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-10T19:53:43-07:00","id":967098,"title":"[5 Things] for a Mage to encounter.","content":"Here's a tool I like to use for game prep. Because there are so many phenomena a Mage PC might run into, I prefer to have a few general details for that category written up in advance, and then glance at that list and improvise when it comes up. I thought that expanding these lists might be a fun forum exercise that anyone can easily contribute to and use themselves.<br /> <br /> These don't need to be in-depth, just brief and evocative with space to take them in a different direction. Depending on the thing, here should be a sense of how it can be used in the scene, and maybe a simple but strong descriptive detail like &quot;wears blue&quot; or &quot;anachronistic&quot; or &quot;animal companion.&quot; They can include references to game traits like particular Merits or Numina, but shouldn't be statted out. The intended use case is &quot;The players have just encountered an unfamiliar X, the ST has nothing planned and needs a skeleton to build from on the fly, so she looks at the list and picks one or two things.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's an example to start us off. Feel free to expand existing lists or create new ones!<br /> <br /> <b>5 Ghosts</b><ul><li>Doesn't realize he's dead: exhausted, sitting on a bench or corner, tries to explain that this is all a misunderstanding and he's only stopped to catch his breath.</li> <li>Twisted into a monster after years of isolation/supernatural influence: obscured face, glowing eyes, rasping voice, long sharp claws.</li> <li>Looking for someone with a trait in common with one of the PCs (dark hair, tattoos, smoking habit) but doesn't remember who the person is.</li> <li>Communicates using EVP, transmitting messages randomly over nearby cell phones and TV screens.</li> <li>Trying to use Numina to recreate the circumstances of their death: house fire, drug overdose, fell and broke their neck, attacked by an animal, etc.</li> </ul><br /> Ideas for expansion: 5 Hallows, 5 Ley Lines, 5 Mystagogues, 5 Familiars, 5 Grimoires...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:04:42-07:00","id":967107,"title":"","content":"5 cursed artifacts<ul><li>A switchblade comb that will brush your hair until you say &quot;comb down&quot;</li> <li>A pillow that tickles you slightly while you sleep, preventing you from resting</li> <li>A locket that compels you to pick it up and wear it until you fall in love. It then drains your mana until you are out, driving you to scour again and again until it's taken all it can. Then and only then, the locket opens, you see that the picture inside is the person you love, laughing at you, and then you throw it away, at which point the next lucky mage picks it up.</li> <li>An iPhone 7</li> <li>A pair of chopsticks that, when you use them to eat, gets the song &quot;chopsticks&quot; stuck in your head and compells you to seek out a piano to play chopsticks. They come in a bright red box and have been re-gifted over five hundred times since 1957.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>International Relations Scholar, Salesman, and GM. Guess which one of those is my favorite?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12305-obrimosmaintenance","name":"ObrimosMaintenance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:46:23-07:00","id":967159,"title":"","content":"5 Hallows<br /> \u200b1-A hallow located in a secure building, crack house or anywhere else where the current residents won't welcome you just dropping in and no, it's not for sale.<br /> 2-A very desirable hallow is located on what used to be the top floor of a very tall building, a building that came down unexpectedly. Now how do you reach it?<br /> 3-A hallow in Times Square or another high traffic location. The tass congeals into small pebbles embedded in the black top. Good luck dodging traffic.<br /> 4-A valuable hallow located in an easily acquired vacant building. Unfortunately it used to be a disco (or line dancing) club and the resonance is...embarrassing. Not to mention ghosts &amp; spirits.<br /> 5-Tried but true...the hallow is located in the same place as a powerful locus and the current residents have...anger issues.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T05:57:27-07:00","id":968470,"title":"","content":"<b>5 urban spirits</b><br /> <br /> 1- A roaring, smoke-belching car spirit, driving crazily and with the acrid smell of spilled booze in it.<br /> <br /> 2- A robot-like ATM machine spirit, with a green-lit screen on his chest, coughing money and surrounded by a cacophony of whispers from wishful and anxious users.<br /> <br /> 3- A huge, feral black cat with eyes filled with electricity and a meow of wailing sirens and construction machines.<br /> <br /> 4- A bum, with skin of newspaper, a filthy long coat, eyes of a pigeon and rats moving inside his skin, murmuring to himself.<br /> <br /> 5- A slouching semaphore, covered in contradictory street signs, communicating through luminous words like 'WALK', 'STOP', 'WATCH', 'KILL', or 'BEHIND_U'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:48:01-07:00","id":968864,"title":"","content":"<b>5 Grimoires</b><br /> <br /> 1. Via Arcana - A grimoire cursed (blessed?) to ensure its magic shall never fade from the Fallen World, the original copy of which was bound and sheathed in chains drawn from Pandemonium itself. Teaching various Matter and Prime rotes, the book is enchanted to curse its readers with a magical compulsion to copy it at least five times and give the copies to their nearest friends. This curse doesn't care if the people the books are given to are Sleepers or Awakened, and the resultant curse plays merry havoc on the former, who are compelled to make unenchanted copies of the book endlessly.<br /> <br /> 2. The Book of the Dead - Containing numerous Death rotes related to accessing the Underworld, the Book of the Dead can also act as a road map to the world of the unliving. Those who follow its grim instructions arrive in a spectral realm resembling the Egyptian afterlife, where Stygian magic flows freely. Is this world a Stygian Emanation Realm? Or something stranger still? What happens to those who are offered a chance to enter the Halls of Osiris if their hearts are successfully weighed?<br /> <br /> 3. Dead Man's Whispers - This grimoire is actually a corpse. A literal corpse, whose mummified flesh is tattooed with Atlantean Runes, and whose sunken eye sockets and wide mouth are luminescent with an ethereal blue light when addressed. The corpse once belonged to a mystagogue who believed their knowledge too valuable to be allowed to fade, and so had their corpse tattooed and preserved, and their ghost chained to the body. Though now ancient and little more than a particularly talkative instruction manual, the ghost has been known to command their corpse to rise and leave the sancta of any Mage it deems to misuse its magic; often shrouding the corpse in illusory spells until it tires out and simply leaves the body where it falls.<br /> <br /> 4. The Scrimshawed Scriptures - Carved into the bones of a whale, the Scrimshawed Scriptures is the affectionate nickname for what stuffier sensibilities call the Mariner's Song. These rotes - written as stories told in song - are supposedly the dreams of sailors driven mad by the mournful ghosts of harpooned whales. Those who learn the rotes find them surprisingly powerful; so long as the rote is cast with the caster vocalizing like a whale - a strange form of inhuman High Speech that the Awakened hear as deep, mournful lowing, and Sleepers hear as due cause to wonder if the Mage is having a stroke - the spell gains an automatic +1 to any factor of the caster's choice.<br /> <br /> However, any Mage who learns these rotes has a price to pay, for each night, they may dream of the Whale Sea; the Astral memory of the oceans themselves and all the whales within it. Such dreams contain many long memories. More than one sorcerer has awoken in a cold sweat, after facing dreams of being crushed between ten-thousand rotting carcasses and sucking in mouthfuls of salty blood when they gasped for air.<br /> <br /> 5. The Carcassone Essay - Light as a feather, the Carcassone Essay is a proper grimoire; written on velum with a quill pen. Written some time in the 12th century, the document is a subtly veiled vision of Hieraconis, as imagined by a French Obrimos monk. Drenched in Christian metaphor, it lovingly describes what it refers to as the Kingdom of the Son of Man, wherein humanity will overcome the &quot;serpents who pretend to the Throne of God&quot; and &quot;false seers will be blinded&quot;. Aside from the usual rhetoric, it contains a number of Prime rotes but, more interesting, it contains a rote which allows the caster to summon an &quot;angelic being&quot;; the same one the caster purports granted upon them this vision. These beings are not spirits, nor are they seemingly called from the Aether. Yet when questioned, they offer a promise of universal salvation and insight on how it might be achieved. What are these strange beings? And are they trustworthy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:43:53-07:00","id":969219,"title":"","content":"<b>5 Mysterious Software Downloads</b><ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=969494#post969494\">An obscure flashlight-App for a cellphone that has a review written in High Speech that claims it projects actual sunlight. Magical inspection with prime, forces or space and tests versus things with vulnerabilities to sunlight proves the review to be accurate. It has no Supernal Magic to dispel...</a></li> <li>There is a Dropbox with a specially modded Minecraft world-download which is a scale model in frighteningly perfect detail of the city the character's are in, and the person dies in game, actually dies in reality during their sleep that night. The Mods increase the difficulty of the game and make things look as realistic as can be expected out of a world built of one meter cubes. The mods require a specific Launcher which makes accessing the world via editors useless, and the difficulty of the modded play is very unforgiving. However for all that danger, Mage Sight interacts with the screen as if both what was on the screen was real and if it also overlapped the place in the real world it represents.</li> <li>A trojan horse ransom-ware that was posing a security program demands, written in High Speech, you agree to send attachments of a digital grimoire to an anonymous email address or your identifying information, which has already been stolen, will be sold to the local Seers of the Throne. (The tech savvy get an IP out of Nigeria, which might just be a proxy server)</li> <li>A facebook puzzle game whose higher levels require High Speech to complete, that rewards digital pet avatar on your wall that require daily feeding(with treats won in the puzzle game), chat interaction, sleeps in several two hour naps a day, which also acts as Familiar in twilight by the computer you won it on. The Familiar can sense any place it is on screen, and scry there.</li> <li>A downward-flowing Matrix-font screensaver acts as a Window to the Hisil for what is behind the display device. Being able to see it requires passive or more focused Mage Sight and Professional Computer skills for dealing with code.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-14-2016, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}